First, the simple one:

	On ULTRIX, you can't produce or use shared libraries.
	End of story.

Second, the other simple one:

	On DEC OSF/1, you don't do anything special with GCC to
	create shared libraries. Read the section 3 of the Programmers
	Guide. Basically, you just create a normal library with all
	the normal flags you're used to. If you later decide that
	the library is to your liking:


		libfoo.a


	Then:

		ld -shared -no_archive -all libfoo.a -none -lc -o libfoo.so

	This example assumes that your shared library in turn is dependent
	only on the C library. If other libraries are needed in turn (say
	the math library), these go into the section after "-none".

		Burkhard Neidecker-Lutz

