 <PATFIELDD@lincoln.cri.nz> wrote:
>We have a DEC 3000 running OSF/1 that won't boot.
>
>The system now only boots to
>...

You can also try to boot to single user mode:

     >>>  boot -fl s

or boot a different kernel:

     >>>  boot -fl s -fi "genvmunix"

Don't forget the quotes, otherwise the system tries 
to boot GENVMUNIX, which doesn't exist.

When in single user mode, do
     #  fsck
     #  mount -u /
     #  mount /usr

Good luck! If that doesn't work, you'll need the OSF/1 CD-ROM.

Siggy Hensel


