|> I am in the directory "/usr/var/adm/crash" and there are a number of
|> files located here... can I delete
|> these files ???

Yes, you can.  The main reason you would want to save them is if you
decide to log a service call regarding the crash.  The memory image and
system image provide a way for the service people to diagnose the cause.

Keep the file "bounds", though.  The contents are an ASCII string
containing a number that limits how many crash dumps the system will
collect.

