Alan gave some suggestions for how to increase the amount of swap area.
I'm just adding a little more information.

|> 2.  Boot the standalone system and increase B to use the D area.
|>     You may be able to do this running single user.

You can do this reasonably easily with the "-e" option to the disklabel
command.  This option will read the disk partition information from the
disk, write it to a file, invoke an editor on the file, and allow you
to change the partition sizes by changing the ASCII representation of
the partitioning information.  When you write the file back out, disklabel
will offer to write the altered information back as new partition
information.  Be VERY CAREFUL when you do this.  DO A BACKUP FIRST!  It's
all too easy to set up partitions incorrectly and destroy the existing
filesystems.  Good luck!

					Frank


