  Attached below are instructions for making shared libraries
  on Sun OS4. Does anyone know what the equivalent instructions
  are on ULTRIX and OSF/1 using gcc?

  E-mail but feel free to post.

  Thanks,

  Emmett
 

   1.  Make for a subroutine/function:

      cc -PIC -c filename.c -o filename.o


   2.  Make the shared library (libtest.so.1.1)

      ld -o libtest.so file1.o file2.o file3.o -assert pure-text

      (Now rename libtest.so to libtest.so.1.1)

   3.  Linking the main program (make sure that libtest is in the LD_LIBRARY_PATH
   during runtime): 

      cc main.o -o a.out -L/yourlibdir -Bdynamic -ltest





