In article <2u23pa$k2f@pdq.coe.montana.edu>, osyjm@cs.montana.edu (Jaye Mathisen) writes:
> 
> Looks to me like the same problems I've had when I accidently configured
> a SCSI device to the same address as the controller.

I've also seen this on a 3000/500 when there's an addressing conflict period
(not the same address as the controller, but the same as some other SCSI
device).  Also, if the CD drive is external, you may want to make sure the SCSI
ID select switch cables are oriented correctly.  Aside from the obvious left to
right orientation, there's also a top and bottom orientation for the two SCSI ID
cables (at least there is on an RRD42, when one of the ID cables has all the
wires pinned together).

Then again, I've seen similar behavior (on an unrelated system/drive combo)
when either the drive, controller, or system (never did figure it out) were
either faulty or incompatible.


