># /sbin/mount -rd /dev/rz4c /mnt
>/dev/rz4c on /mnt: No valid filesystem exists on this partition
> The cd disk that we want to mount is the Alpha Freeware CD.
>
>we check, the device by:
># file /dev/rrz*c
>/dev/rrz0c:     character special (8/2) SCSI #0 RZxx disk #0 (SCSI ID #0)
>/dev/rrz4c:     character special (8/4098) SCSI #0 RRD42 disk #32 (SCSI ID #4)
>
>then we remove /dev/rz4* and 
># cd /dev
># MAKEDEV rz4
>MAKEDEV: special file(s) for rz4:
>rz4a rz4b rz4c rz4d rz4e rz4f rz4g rz4h
>
>but still,
># /sbin/mount -rd /dev/rz4c /mnt
>/dev/rz4c on /mnt: No valid filesystem exists on this partition
>
>
lihsin;

  The Alpha Freeware CD is ISO9660 format. Use the command:

	mount -t cdfs -r -o nodefperm /dev/rz4c /mnt

  You must have the ISO9660 support compiled in the kernel for this
to work. You must have the line:

options         CDFS

in your /sys/conf/'SYSTEM-NAME-IN-UPPERCASE' configuration file.

Craig
