The X server also grows in 1.3. All you have to do is configure it so
that it terminates (and restarts) each time someone logs out.
To do this you can for instance change the ':0' line in
/usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers to

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -bs -su -terminate

With this the X server stays below 9MB on my recently upgraded 2.0
system. 

BTW: 2.0 uses a lot less memory than 1.3. No reason not to upgrade. 
I upgraded without any problems. Had to recompile gcc and emacs,
though...

