8 KB is the only block size supported by UFS.  I think it is also the
only block size supported by the Advanced File System.  ULTRIX supported
a 4 KB block, but would have wasted the same amount of space.  I also
have wonder where you get the 10% number.

A 110 KB file will use 13 3/4 8 KB blocks.  Since the file system will
want to allocate full 8 KB blocks at that point, an extra 2 KB per file
will be allocated.  2 KB out of 110 KB is 1.82% not 10%.

If you are thinking of the 10% reserved space, that has nothing to
do with the block size.  You can also change that with tunefs(8).
If your data is read-mostly, then careful creation of the file
system will probably let you lower it to a smaller value.

