I've talked with several other folks at different sites who confirmed
my problems with lk401 Rev C keyboards.  Their solution was to
have DEC hardware support replace the keyboards.

I've talked with "Bruce from the Ultrix/OSF1" software support group
who suggests having hardware support replace the keyboards.

My conclusion is that Rev C LK401 keyboards do not work properly with
OSF1 V1.3 or V2.0.  I suspect that there may also be a problem with Ultrix
as well, but I've not yet confirmed it.

If you obtain a Rev C keyboard with your alpha/AXP/OSF workstation,
you may want to consider getting it replaced with a Rev A keyboard
at your earliest convenience.

I do not know if anyone at DEC
	- knows about this problem (other than the software support person I talked to)
	- is working on a software solution to this problem.

I would not be surprised by an official DEC response of
"This problem may be fixed in a future release."

Other than that, I'm pretty impressed with these workstations.

