To determine if the kernel table sizes are adequate, I usually look at
table usage via 'pstat -T.'  The following is an example of the output
under a ULTRIX 4.3a system.

 457/3835	files
 731/2684	gnodes
 305/2080	processes
  53/ 221/ 300	active/reclaimable/total texts
 124/4587	00k swap

If the tables are near capacity, then I usually increase the maxusers option
