stan@chirpa.mayo.edu (Andrew Staniszewski) writes:


>yes,
>DEC added a prototype for sbrk in V2.0, which was not prototyped in V1.3,
>and then they decided, I think as a practicle joke, to  prototype it as 
>returning (char *) instead of (void *), just to be differnt, especially 
>from the original documentation, but in particular from what the rest 
>of the world prototypes sbrk to be ....

You'll be relieved that we "saw the light" and in V3.0 have made
this change:

 * 	Changed the declaration of sbrk() from extern char * to extern
 * 	void *.  Fixes OSF_QARs #18324 and #20165.

Apologies in advance to all you folks who changed things to expect
char * and get to change back!

Note also:

 * 	Change argument of sbrk from int to ssize_t.

i.e.:

typedef unsigned long   size_t;
