In article <2sivv7$833@jeeves.niehs.nih.gov> bob@niehs.nih.gov (Bob Nance) writes:

   I have, indeed built CAP60pl192 on an OSF/1 v2.0 box. After applying all
   of the patches, I had only to make on other change...

   For some reason, the ./Configure process sets up the gen.makes to create
   a makefile in the ./support/ethertalk directory that includes a line that
   says:

   POBJS=spfiltp.o pfopen.o

   When this section builds, the pfopen.o is not build and the make fails.
   I removed the pfopen.o and the make was succesful, and, most importantly,
   the system worked (pfopen is is a system call that already exists on the
   Alpha when the PACKETFILTER option is installed in the kernel).

The reason, I believe, for this, is that under V1.3 of OSF/1, the
pfopen *library* call wasn't in the standard C library.  You were
meant to copy the source code from /usr/examples/packetfilter/pfopen.c
into the support/ethertalk directory.  It appears that under V2.0
pfopen is now in the standard C library so this shouldn't be
neccesary.

Ray.

