this is almost always due to heap corruption in you application. A 
possible culprit would be something like:

	unsigned long = (undsigned long)malloc(4);

A good way of fixing these is to use a debugging malloc pacakage
such as the one found via anonymous ftp at:

	gatekeeper.pa.dec.com:/pub/misc/malloc_dbg/*.tar.gz

be sure to read the info in ./contrib/dec_notes that is in the tar
file.




