We had that problem as well.  There may well still be problems along
these lines, but one thing I discovered is that DEC OSF1 has two options
for swapping, and the default one is a real hog for your swap space.
The method can be changed by removing the symbolic link "/sbin/swapdefault".
This is of course not documented or refered to in any way in the UNIX
manual pages provided with OSF.  Thanks a lot DEC.  See your paper documents
for more specific information.

If anyone from the DEC OSF team is reading this, PLEASE document the
basics of all system features in the UNIX manual pages.  Putting more
detailed, tutorial-style, and long-winded explanations in vendor-specific
documents is great, but minimal explanations of ALL system files and
program options should go into the on-line UNIX manual pages.  These
should have enough concise information for an expert to get the job
done.  Right now there's a lot of "See such-and-such-a-document to
find any useful information at all", and at least this one very
important piece of system configuration information (swapdefault)
that is not even hinted at _anywhere_ in the manuals!

Andrew Draskoy
