I suspect this also caused a couple of panic's on our OSF/1 2.0 Alpha
here. From reading the runes I guess the sequence of events to be
something along the lines of:

Someone tries to start a process
Kernel tries to pre-allocate swap for it
Kernel finds no swap available to pre-allocate
Kernel tries to kill process
Whilst signalling the process the kernel tries to allocate some memory
The alloc fails
The kernel panic's

crash + burn :-(

Since I've turned off DECs braindead swap preallocation we've not had a
recurrence of it.

